      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale Stream API\n\nWelcome to the CloudScale Stream API. Follow these steps to set up your environment, obtain an API key, and make your first authenticated GET request.\n\n## Getting an API Key\n\n1. Sign up on the CloudScale Stream website using your preferred web browser.\n2. Access your account dashboard and navigate to the \"API Keys\" section.\n3. Click \"Create a New Key\" and follow the on-screen instructions to complete the setup.\n4. Record your new API key securely, as it will be needed later.\n\n## Preparing Your Development Environment\n\n1. Install the CloudScale Stream SDK for your desired programming language from our [official documentation](#).\n2. Import the SDK into your project and set up basic connectivity with required credentials.\n\n## Making Your First Authenticated GET Request\n\n- Utilize the credentials from your API key to authenticate your requests.\n- Create a GET request to the desired endpoint and include your API key in the request headers for authentication.\n- Await the response and verify the data output from your GET request.\n\nBy following these simple steps, you'll be ready to take full advantage of our CloudScale Stream API capabilities!",
